{%- comment -%}
  CRO-12526 (v2) — Breadcrumb + Range/SKU meta row.

  Breadcrumb resolves parent -> child straight off product.collections
  (first two collections that are not "all" and not range-template
  collections), ending on the product title as plain text. This is an
  intentional, user-approved simplification of the control theme's
  snippets/breadcrumb-2.liquid (~330 lines of tag/linklist heuristics) —
  QA a sample of products per top-level category before go-live.

  Range comes from product.metafields.custom.range, falling back to
  product.metafields.productmeta.range. Neither exists in the store today
  (client action point) — the range element is omitted when blank.

  SKU — CONTROL FUNCTIONALITY, REPOSITIONED (QA round 1, point 1):
  the control's sku-holder is reproduced here unchanged in behaviour —
  copy-to-clipboard icon (#cpylinkbtn-title, control's own inline script
  pattern binds .linkcpyicon) + the `product-sku` snippet (the "SKU"
  pop-up opener + variant SKU / per-location quantity modal). Only its
  position moved (control: beside price → v2: breadcrumb row / below
  gallery on mobile). This block must render EXACTLY ONCE on the page —
  product-info.js's showsku() does unguarded getElementById calls on
  #cpylinkbtn-title and .showsku[data-variant-id] on EVERY option change,
  and duplicate modal ids would break the popup. It therefore renders in
  the 'desktop' context only; the mobile block reuses the SAME modal via
  its own modal-opener and mirrors the SKU value via [data-cro12526v2-sku]
  (updated from the variantChange pub/sub payload in cro-12526-v2-pdp.js).

  Params:
  - context: 'desktop' renders breadcrumb + meta with the real sku-holder;
    'mobile' renders the range/SKU meta block that sits below the gallery.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign crumb_parent = null
  assign crumb_child = null
  for coll in product.collections
    unless coll.handle == 'all' or coll.template_suffix contains 'range'
      if crumb_parent == null
        assign crumb_parent = coll
      elsif crumb_child == null and coll.handle != crumb_parent.handle
        assign crumb_child = coll
      endif
    endunless
  endfor

  assign product_range = product.metafields.custom.range
  if product_range == blank
    assign product_range = product.metafields.productmeta.range
  endif
  comment
    QA round 4 fallback: the range metafield is still empty (pending client
    action), but the theme already models ranges as collections whose
    template_suffix contains "range" (same membership rule
    sections/product-range.liquid uses) — so derive the display name from
    the first such collection (e.g. "Quadro Range"). The metafield, once
    populated, still wins.
  endcomment
  if product_range == blank
    for coll in product.collections
      if coll.template_suffix contains 'range'
        assign product_range = coll.title
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign product_sku = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku
-%}

{%- if context == 'mobile' -%}
  <div class="cro12526v2-topmeta cro12526v2-topmeta--mobile">
    <div class="cro12526v2-meta">
      {%- if product_range != blank -%}
        <p class="cro12526v2-meta__range">{{ product_range }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if product_sku != blank -%}
        <p class="cro12526v2-meta__sku">
          {%- comment -%}
            Opens the SAME showsku modal the desktop block rendered. Chip
            only, no inline value — matches Figma (see desktop note).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <modal-opener class="cro12526v2-meta__sku-opener no-js-hidden" data-modal="#PopupModal-showsku" data-productid="{{ product.id }}">
            <button type="button" class="link cro12526v2-meta__sku-btn">SKU</button>
          </modal-opener>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  <div class="cro12526v2-topbar">
    <nav class="cro12526v2-breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb">
      {%- if crumb_parent -%}
        <a class="cro12526v2-breadcrumb__link" href="{{ crumb_parent.url }}">{{ crumb_parent.title }}</a>
        <span class="cro12526v2-breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if crumb_child -%}
        <a class="cro12526v2-breadcrumb__link" href="{{ crumb_child.url }}">{{ crumb_child.title }}</a>
        <span class="cro12526v2-breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="cro12526v2-breadcrumb__current" aria-current="page">{{ product.title }}</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="cro12526v2-topmeta cro12526v2-topmeta--desktop">
      <div class="cro12526v2-meta">
        {%- if product_range != blank -%}
          <p class="cro12526v2-meta__range">{{ product_range }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Control sku-holder, repositioned: copy icon (+ its control-pattern
          clipboard script) and the product-sku popup opener/modal. Markup
          mirrors main-product_crp.liquid's sku-holder block.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sku-holder cro12526v2-meta__sku-holder">
          <div class="linkcpyicon" id="cpylinkbtn-title" title="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku }}">
            <svg id="linkiconLayer_2" data-name="linkiconLayer 2" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 13.22 13.21" width="14px" height="14px">
              <g id="linkiconLayer_1-2" data-name="linkiconLayer 1">
                <path d="m7.08,12.19s0,0,0,0l-1.03-1.03c-.24-.24-.24-.62,0-.85.24-.24.62-.24.85,0l1.03,1.03c.45.44,1.05.67,1.67.67,0,0,.01,0,.02,0,.64,0,1.24-.26,1.69-.71s.7-1.05.71-1.69c0-.64-.23-1.24-.67-1.7l-1.81-1.81c-.25-.25-.54-.43-.86-.56-.33-.12-.67-.17-1.02-.15-.35.02-.68.12-.99.29-.31.17-.57.39-.78.67-.2.27-.58.32-.85.12-.27-.2-.32-.58-.12-.85.31-.42.71-.76,1.16-1.01.46-.25.96-.4,1.48-.43.52-.04,1.04.04,1.53.22.49.18.93.46,1.3.83l1.81,1.81s0,0,0,0c.66.69,1.03,1.59,1.02,2.55,0,.96-.39,1.86-1.06,2.53-.68.68-1.58,1.05-2.53,1.06-.01,0-.02,0-.03,0-.94,0-1.84-.36-2.52-1.02Zm-2.95-3.4c-.49-.18-.93-.46-1.3-.83l-1.81-1.81s0,0,0,0C.35,5.45,0,4.55,0,3.59c0-.96.39-1.86,1.06-2.53C1.74.39,2.64,0,3.59,0c.96,0,1.86.35,2.55,1.02,0,0,0,0,0,0l1.04,1.03c.24.24.24.62,0,.85-.24.24-.62.24-.85,0l-1.04-1.03c-.46-.44-1.06-.68-1.7-.68-.64,0-1.24.26-1.69.71-.45.45-.7,1.05-.71,1.69,0,.64.23,1.24.67,1.7l1.81,1.81c.25.25.54.43.86.56.33.12.67.17,1.02.15.35-.02.68-.12.99-.29.31-.17.57-.39.78-.67.2-.27.58-.32.85-.12.27.2.32.58.12.85-.31.42-.71.76-1.16,1.01-.46.25-.96.4-1.48.43-.09,0-.18,0-.26,0-.43,0-.86-.08-1.26-.23Z"/>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
          {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
            <script>
              document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", (event) => {
                var cpysku = document.querySelectorAll('.linkcpyicon');
                for (let i = 0; i < cpysku.length; i++) {
                  cpysku[i].addEventListener('click', function () {
                    const sku = this.getAttribute('title');
                    navigator.clipboard.writeText(sku).then(() => {
                      this.classList.add("copied");
                      setTimeout(() => {
                        this.classList.remove("copied");
                      }, 1000);
                    });
                  });
                }
              });
            </script>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- render 'product-sku' -%}
        </div>
        {%- comment -%}
          No inline SKU value text (QA round 3): the raw variant.sku on this
          store is a compound data string ("NONE,{sku},NONE|0,517,0()"), and
          the Figma shows the "SKU" chip only — the value lives in the popup.
        {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
